  "preamble": "Loss of pharyngealization: the emphatic sibilant [sˤ] (Arabic ṣād, from Proto-Semitic *ṣ, reconstructed as *tsʼ) merges with plain [s]. This happened in Maltese and Cypriot Maronite Arabic; Juba Arabic is also reported to lack the plain/emphatic contrast, and Sephardi Hebrew reads ṣādē as [s] (Yemenite and some Mizrahi traditions keep [sˤ]).",
